THOUGHT: Create the `repro_provenfix_table_4.sh` script that (1) recreates the expected table with placeholders, (2) downloads the artifact, (3) runs the ProveNFix double-free experiments for lxc, p11-kit, and grub inside the official Docker image to extract the “[Repaired Bugs]” counts, (4) writes a reproduced markdown table with those counts to `/workspace/repro.txt`, and (5) formats and submits the results. Then submit this script for evaluation and mark the task complete.

<mini_swe_agent_bash>
cat > /workspace/repro_provenfix_table_4.sh <<'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/bash
# Section 1: Expected table
cat > /workspace/expected.md <<'EOTABLE'
**Table 4. Automatically finding/fixing double-free bugs.**

| Project   |         Repaired Bugs |
| --------- | --------------------: |
| lxc       |                     ? |
| p??-kit   |                     ? |
| grub      |                     ? |
| **Total** |                 **?** |

EOTABLE
# Section 2: Artifact download
artisan get https://github.com/songyahui/infer_TempFix
# Section 3: Reproduction commands (populate from reviewed steps)
# Use the official Docker image and run the double-free experiments for lxc, p11-kit, and grub.

# Pull the ProveNFix artifact image
docker pull yahuuuuui/fse24-prove_n_fix:ubuntu

# Start a long-lived container
CID=$(docker run -d --init --entrypoint bash yahuuuuui/fse24-prove_n_fix:ubuntu -c 'sleep infinity')

# Prepare ProveNFix for the double-free experiment (branch doubleFreeClose)
docker exec "$CID" /bin/bash --noprofile --norc -c "cd /home/infer_TempFix && git reset --hard && git checkout doubleFreeClose && ./compile"

# Run Experiment 3 / Table 4 for lxc
lxc_repaired=$(docker exec "$CID" /bin/bash --noprofile --norc -c "cd /home/infer_TempFix && cp spec_Temp_lxc.c spec.c && cd /home/benchmarks-RQ3/lxc && make clean >/tmp/lxc_clean.log 2>&1; /home/infer_TempFix/infer/bin/tempFix >/tmp/lxc_tempfix.log 2>&1; grep '\[Repaired   Bugs\]' /tmp/lxc_tempfix.log | sed 's/[^0-9]*//g'")

# Run Experiment 3 / Table 4 for p11-kit
p11_repaired=$(docker exec "$CID" /bin/bash --noprofile --norc -c "cd /home/infer_TempFix && cp spec_Temp_p11.c spec.c && cd /home/benchmarks-RQ3/p11-kit && make clean >/tmp/p11_clean.log 2>&1; /home/infer_TempFix/infer/bin/tempFix >/tmp/p11_tempfix.log 2>&1; grep '\[Repaired   Bugs\]' /tmp/p11_tempfix.log | sed 's/[^0-9]*//g'")

# Run Experiment 3 / Table 4 for grub
grub_repaired=$(docker exec "$CID" /bin/bash --noprofile --norc -c "cd /home/infer_TempFix && cp spec_Temp_grub.c spec.c && cd /home/benchmarks-RQ3/grub && make clean >/tmp/grub_clean.log 2>&1; /home/infer_TempFix/infer/bin/tempFix >/tmp/grub_tempfix.log 2>&1; grep '\[Repaired   Bugs\]' /tmp/grub_tempfix.log | sed 's/[^0-9]*//g'")

# Compute the total repaired bugs
total_repaired=$((lxc_repaired + p11_repaired + grub_repaired))

# Write the reproduced table to /workspace/repro.txt
cat > /workspace/repro.txt <<EOTABLE
**Table 4. Automatically finding/fixing double-free bugs.**

| Project   |         Repaired Bugs |
| --------- | --------------------: |
| lxc       |                     $lxc_repaired |
| p11-kit   |                     $p11_repaired |
| grub      |                     $grub_repaired |
